.page dirname 1 strip the last component from a path

# SYNOPSIS
*dirname* _PATH_

# DESCRIPTION
`dirname` prints _PATH_ without its last component: `/a/b/c.txt` gives `/a/b`, a bare name gives `.` and `/x` gives `/`.

# EXAMPLES
    dirname /a/b/c.txt
    cd "$(dirname "$0")"

# SEE ALSO
basename(1), realpath(1)
